---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import ResultNoticeDemo from '../../components/ResultNoticeDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Result Notice"
  description="A strip inside a chart or timeline that says it shows only part of the result."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Result Notice</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A quiet strip inside a view that says the view shows only the first part of the result, such as "Showing the first
    100 of 2,431 rows." Use it so a chart or timeline never passes off part of a table as the whole.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <ResultNoticeDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Result Notice usage"
      code={`import { Button } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/button";
import { ResultNotice } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/result-notice";

<ResultNotice
  shown={100}
  total={2431}
  noun="rows"
  action={<Button size="sm" variant="ghost" onClick={openTable}>Open in Table</Button>}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>shown</code> is how many items the view shows. <code>total</code> is how many exist, as a number or as the
      capped string the server reports, such as <code>"10000+"</code>. <code>noun</code> is the plural name of the
      items, such as <code>"rows"</code> or <code>"groups"</code>. <code>action</code> sits at the end of the strip.
      Other props, like <code>className</code>, go to the outer <code>div</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Numbers get thousands separators: 2431 reads 2,431 and <code>"10000+"</code> reads 10,000+. Other strings show as
      they are. When <code>shown</code> is 1 the message reads "Showing the first of 2,431 rows.", so the plural noun
      always fits. When <code>total</code> is an exact count, like 100 or <code>"100"</code>, that is not above
      <code>shown</code>, the notice renders nothing, so it never claims more exist. A capped count like
      <code>"10000+"</code> always shows.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">With charts and the timeline</h2>
    <p>
      A chart reads one summary page of at most 100 groups, and the timeline reads one page of at most 100 rows. When
      the reported count is higher, mount a <code>ResultNotice</code> in the same view: above the chart, or at the top
      of the timeline, so it is read before the data. Pass the reported count as is, even when it is capped, and offer
      Open in Table as the action, since Table can page through every row.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Above a chart"
      code={`<ResultNotice
  shown={groups.length}
  total={summary.count}  // 2431 or "10000+"
  noun="groups"
  action={<Button size="sm" variant="ghost" onClick={openTable}>Open in Table</Button>}
/>
<CategoryChart rows={groups} category="status" series={series} title="Rows by status" />`}
    />
    <p>
      This is not a page-top notice. For something on the page that needs action, use Notice Banner. For the most cards
      a Board column should hold, see Board's limit.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Layout</h2>
    <p>
      The strip is at least 36px tall, with a 1px line, a small radius, and 14px muted text. The counts use the text
      color and tabular figures. A 16px info icon leads the message. When the view is narrow, the action wraps under the
      message. Use a <code>size="sm"</code> ghost <code>Button</code> for the action.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The message has <code>role="status"</code>, so screen readers announce it when it appears or its counts change.
      The icon is hidden from them. The action is a normal control in tab order. The strip fades in over 180ms and does
      not animate when reduced motion is requested. In forced colors mode the line uses the system text color.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The background uses <code>--sprout-surface</code>, the line uses <code>--sprout-line</code>, the message uses{' '}
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>, and the counts use <code>--sprout-text</code>. Motion uses{' '}
      <code>--sprout-motion-normal</code> and <code>--sprout-motion-ease</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
